and nearly a billion times during the course of his 30-year professional career.

198
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:47,740
There's no point.

199
00:22:48,070 --> 00:22:52,410
part of the human body that likely sees these kinds of collision forces and shearing stresses,

200
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:56,750
which is why vocal folds essentially wear out over time.

201
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,750
It's also why just months earlier, damaged vocal calls canceled much of Aerosmith's tour.

202
00:23:05,090 --> 00:23:07,760
Tyler could barely sing.

203
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:15,100
forcing him to undergo Zeitels' knife, or laser in this case.

204
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:20,770
Stephen basically had a vocal bleed, which is very common in performers.

205
00:23:24,770 --> 00:23:26,780
common in fact to many with a gift of gab,

206
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:28,440
from attorneys to telemarketers.

207
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:34,450
The laser surgery, which Zeitels and his team pioneered,

208
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:40,790
works by sealing off damaged vessels to stop the bleeding.

209
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:43,790
This is Stephen Tyler's voice box,

210
00:23:44,130 --> 00:23:48,800
and these are his fragile blood vessels disappearing.

211
