vocal chords spring into action.

215
00:24:13,490 --> 00:24:15,830
This is Stephen Tyler outside.

216
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:25,840
Every time that I look in the mirror, always...

217
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:33,410
Every time we exhale,

218
00:24:35,510 --> 00:24:39,520
we force air through our two membranous vocal cords. When we bring them together,

219
00:24:39,850 --> 00:24:41,850
they vibrate.

220
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:53,530
These vibrations produce sound, much like a guitar string after it's been plucked.

